Package: fastlpr
Title: Fast Local Polynomial Regression and Kernel Density Estimation
Version: 1.0.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Ying", "Wang", email = "yingwangrigel@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Min", "Li", email = "minli.231314@gmail.com", role = "aut")
    )
Author: Ying Wang [aut, cre], Min Li [aut]
Maintainer: Ying Wang <yingwangrigel@gmail.com>
Description: NUFFT-accelerated local polynomial regression and kernel density estimation
    for large, scattered, or complex-valued datasets. Provides automatic bandwidth
    selection via Generalized Cross-Validation (GCV) for regression and Likelihood
    Cross-Validation (LCV) for density estimation. This is the R port of the fastLPR
    MATLAB/Python toolbox, achieving O(N + M log M) computational complexity through
    custom Non-Uniform Fast Fourier Transform implementation with Gaussian gridding.
    Supports 1D/2D/3D data, complex-valued responses, heteroscedastic variance estimation,
    and confidence interval computation. Performance optimized with vectorized R code
    and compiled helpers via Rcpp/RcppArmadillo.
